MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

As another proponent of using Eigen::Matrix more, I'll also chime in here.  For me, the big win is in making the code under stan/mcmc much cleaner.  Perhaps even more significantly, Hessians in std::vector's are, at best, very awkward and error prone.  Add in the need to do matrix-vector ops, invert or take matrix exponentials with Hessians and functions of Hessians, std::vectors fall down almost completely and are likely to be slow.

Cheers,
Marcus

