Yeah, it's true, it's a pretty pervasive change.

Maybe one strategy is to start at the bottom (functions which don't pass vectors on to other functions) and work your way up may be best since it's easy to efficiently go from std::vector -> to an Eigen::Matrix with an Eigen::Map.  This way it could be done piecemeal and won't block a release or other peoples work.  Until it's all done it may be somewhat inefficient, but hopefully not too big of a hit.

Cheers,
Marcus

