I really need to work on supporting user plugins
of any kind.  Like a lot of these improvements, it
shouldn't be that hard to code.

The main issue is getting function declarations going.
I don't want to just parse any old thing into C++ so
that the C++ compiler won't crash on users.

I take it the reason you like the function chaining is
that it doesn't have to upconvert the intermediate
expression templates back to Matrix?  To exploit that,
the user would have to understand the Eigen expression
templates so as to return appropriate values.   The
declaration in Stan could still be Matrix in this case
because all the expression templates are assignable to
Matrix.

- Bob

