After some discussion on the dev list, Matt correctly
guessed there was a zero in the data being modeled as
beta distributed, which I repeat here, with the zero in the
first line of data highlighted.

   O <-
   structure(c(0.7, 0.2, 0.55, 0.2, 0.5, 0, 0.42, 0.4, 0.3, 0.8, 0.74, 0.6, 0.72,
                                         ^
   0.19, 0.58, 0.18, 0.48, 0.01, 0.45, 0.48, 0.4, 0.85, 0.75, 0.68, 0.69, 0.26,
   0.54, 0.19, 0.55, 0.05, 0.44, 0.49, 0.35, 0.78, 0.71, 0.69, 0.68, 0.24, 0.52,
   0.21, 0.51, 0.04, 0.46, 0.5, 0.38, 0.81, 0.7, 0.7, 0.71, 0.35, 0.51, 0.22, 0.52,
   0.03, 0.43, 0.51, 0.39, 0.82, 0.72, 0.71),
   .Dim = c(4, 3, 5))

I don't know there's much we can do to fix this issue.  An actual 0 is
outside the proper support for the beta distribution.

- Bob

